# Pantomina — Update Docs With the Code

When the user asks to implement, fix, ship, or update something, treat documentation as part of the same change. Do not wait to be asked.

## Same pass

1. Change the code (or other impacted files).
2. Update every log that the change affects.

## Files to check (only what the change touches)

| File | When to update |
|---|---|
| `docs/DECISIONS.md` | New lock, supersede, or conscious phase skip — dated row + Why |
| `APP_SPEC.md` | Product, phase acceptance, or stack change |
| `docs/app-store-checklist.md` | Builds, review, or submission status |
| `README.md` | How to run, phase status, privacy/network claims |
| `docs/SKILLS_REVIEW.md` | Only if revisiting the approved review |

## Style

- Match existing table and bullet format. Include **Why** on decision-log rows.
- Skip a file if nothing in it changed.

## Do not

- Ship code-only and offer docs later unless the user explicitly says so.
- Invent new log files beyond the table above without asking.
